# A weather code nobody has seen before.
#
# The glyph comes from `iconCode`, not from the condition text. ECCC publishes
# 0 to 48 today, and the feed is one they label experimental, so a code outside
# that set is a question of when rather than whether.
#
# What must happen: the label keeps the condition and the temperature and draws
# no glyph. Not a fallback picture, and not a question mark. The rule reads
# `condition · temp`, and a stand-in glyph would sit beside a `·` and read as a
# character in its own right, so the honest answer is to draw nothing.
#
# The temperature is below zero here as well, which is the other half of this
# label: a minus sign in a field the rule right-aligns against the terminal.
cache ../cache.db
date 2026-09-11
time 08:00
offset -04:00
size 100 14

# One screen is enough. The rule carries the weather on every screen, so a
# second frame of it proves nothing the first did not.
enter
